rsity and potential for creative manipulation. It also considers division, which may open a path to forming intermediate values (like 8 from 25–22–3 or via fractions), making it more promising than the others.\n- While all approaches are flawed in execution (e.g., no actual valid expression is formed), they all show correct reasoning about scale and proximity to the target.\n\nThe most promising approach is i3 because it:\n- Identifies a close product (59×16 = 944),\n- Explicitly attempts to build 16 from available numbers (2×8),\n- Considers using division (e.g., 84/2 = 42) to generate intermediate values,\n- Shows a more structured and diverse exploration of operations (multiplication, division, subtraction),\n- Has the highest potential to lead to a valid solution through further refinement.\n\ni0 and i1 are redundant, as they follow the same path with minimal variation. i2 is similar but less focused on building intermediate values.\n\nThus, the most unique and promising approach is i3, and it is the only one that demonstrates a clear path forward with creative use of operations.\n\n<results>\ni3\n</results>"]
